<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">alchemy</ansi> (skill)

Alchemy is the craft of combining herbs, reagents, and vessels into consumable preparations
— potions, salves, poultices, and draughts. Results range from basic healing to more exotic
effects. The skill is governed by <ansi fg="yellow">Perception</ansi>, since precision and careful observation
matter more than brute force.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Requirements ━━━</ansi>

  Station:   An <ansi fg="yellow">alchemy_bench</ansi> must be in the room with you.
             The Alchemist's Workshop is west of Training Grounds in Startland.
  Materials: Herbs, plant matter, and empty vessels such as vials.
             Find them on the ground in the Workshop or loot feral herbalists.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Known Recipes ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Healing Poultice</ansi>    Skill 0   2x healers-root, 1x cloth-strip              2 rounds
  <ansi fg="yellow">Stamina Draught</ansi>     Skill 0   2x bitter-thistle, 1x small-vial             2 rounds
  <ansi fg="yellow">Conviction Draught</ansi>  Skill 3   1x healers-root, 1x bitter-thistle, 1x small-vial  2 rounds

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Using Consumables ━━━</ansi>

Crafted potions and poultices are used with the <ansi fg="command">drink</ansi> command:

  <ansi fg="command">drink poultice</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">drink draught</ansi>

They apply their effect immediately. Check <ansi fg="command">inventory</ansi> to see what you are carrying,
and <ansi fg="command">conditions</ansi> to see active effects.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Skill Progression ━━━</ansi>

Alchemy improves through use. Each completed craft attempt (success or failure) has a
chance to advance the skill. Alchemy progresses faster per use than combat skills because
crafting opportunities are less frequent.

There is no trainer for alchemy — practice is the only teacher.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Commands ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">craft list</ansi>          Show all recipes, including alchemy ones, with status.
  <ansi fg="command">craft <recipe></ansi>      Begin crafting an alchemy recipe.
  <ansi fg="command">drink <item></ansi>        Consume a crafted potion or poultice.
  <ansi fg="command">skills</ansi>              Check your current alchemy skill level.

